.TH petsitter 1  "petsitter 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
petsitter \- Walk all your AI coding agents on one leash: a live terminal view of every Claude Code, Codex and opencode session in a folder.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpetsitter\fR [\fB\-\-idle\fR] [\fB\-\-exited\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-\-view\fR] [\fB\-\-once\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIROOT\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Keep an eye on every AI coding agent session running under a directory.
.PP
Sessions of Claude Code, Codex and opencode whose working directory is ROOT or one of its descendants are shown live, in a tree of their folders.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-idle\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 10m]
Mark live sessions as quiet after this long without activity
.TP
\fB\-\-exited\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 12h]
Keep exited sessions listed for this long
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 2s]
Maximum delay between refreshes when no file change is detected
.TP
\fB\-\-view\fR \fI<VIEW>\fR [default: tree]
Screen layout
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
tree: Machine and quotas on top, sessions in a tree of folders, details of the selected session or git folder docked at the bottom
.IP \(bu 2
flat: A borderless list, one line per session
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-once\fR
Print the sessions once as plain text and exit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIROOT\fR]
Directory to monitor, usually the parent of your repositories [default: current directory]
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
petsitter\-hooks(1)
Manage optional agent hooks that report approval prompts
.TP
petsitter\-doctor(1)
Check terminal color detection and the optional integrations
.TP
petsitter\-man(1)
Write the man pages into a directory
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
